&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kikoff: The Fintech Powering Financial Security at Scale&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Kikoff is a profitable, pre-IPO fintech company on a mission to empower everyone to achieve financial security. With record revenue growth in 2025 and a unicorn valuation, we&#39;ve built a suite of products that help millions of people build credit, access liquidity, and save money.&lt;br&gt;We&#39;re scaling fast. Join us if you want to build something meaningful and help millions of people move forward financially.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Kikoff:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a consumer fintech startup, and you will be working with serial entrepreneurs who have built strong consumer brands and innovative products. We value extreme ownership, clear communication, a strong sense of craftsmanship, and the desire to create lasting work and work relationships. Yes, you can build an exciting business AND have real-life real-customer impact.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an Affiliate Marketing Manager to join our Business team. This isn’t just a &quot;client-facing&quot; role; it’s a hybrid of digital marketing strategy and data analysis. You will own a set of partners, define growth strategy and optimization paths, and collaborate closely with the User Acquisition team on achieving growth goals.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll own&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Northstar Objectives:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion Kikoff’s products and services and become the influential main point of contact for our active partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define Kikoff and Grant’s ambitious new user acquisition goals through account management, up/cross selling, product roadmap recommendations, and optimizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consistently overachieve monthly acquisition goals and grow your career as a contributing member of Kikoff&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Affiliate Relationship Management:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the main point of contact for assigned affiliate partners, fostering strong and collaborative relationships and actively source and onboard net new partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate regularly with affiliates partners to understand their needs, provide support, and address any concerns or issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a liaison between affiliates and internal teams to ensure alignment on goals, promotions, and campaign strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide support to existing and inquiring partners while building out scalable systems to support common partner needs&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and run new verticals and partner types, prioritize outbound targets by expected volume and fit, and take partners from outreach to live and performing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attend major partner conferences to foster affiliate relationships, find new partnership opportunities, and represent Kikoff externally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Campaign Management and Optimization:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Align partner strategy with User Acquisition goals and set clear roadmaps for achieving volume and quality KPIs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with affiliate partners to develop and execute effective marketing campaigns that drive traffic, conversions, and revenue&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor campaign performance, analyze data, and identify opportunities for optimization and improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present strategic guidance and recommendations to partners to help them maximize their performance and reach their goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Marketing, Business, or related field preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3-4 years of experience in affiliate marketing, account management, or a related role with at least 2 years owning a partner book or channel with a budget&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of affiliate marketing principles, strategies, and best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience negotiating performance deals and can clearly articulate deal-making approach&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication, writing, and interpersonal skills, with the ability to build rapport and trust with affiliate partners and cross-functional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable building a volume/budget forecast and an approach to achieve it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to manage multiple projects and priorities in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical mindset with the ability to interpret data, draw insights, and make data-driven decisions; proficiency with data software such as Tableau and Amplitude&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with affiliate tracking platforms and tools (e.g., Impact, Appsflyer), proficiency in Excel/Google Sheets (Pivot Tables, VLOOKUPs), and familiarity with AI automation (Claude Cowork, Claude Code)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-motivated, proactive, and results-oriented, with a commitment to delivering exceptional service and results and brings a “test and learn” approach&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with DTC, subscription, or fintech a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Base Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$110,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$125,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A note on applying:&lt;/strong&gt; We know great candidates sometimes hold back if they don’t meet every qualification listed. If you’re excited about this role and believe you can do the work, we encourage you to apply. We’re looking for capability and trajectory, not a perfect checklist match.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;Equal Employment Opportunity Statement&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Kikoff Inc. is an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to complying with all federal, state, and local laws providing equal employment opportunities and considers qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, creed, gender, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy, sex, gender expression or identity, sexual orientation, citizenship, or any other legally protected class.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please reference the following for &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.eeoc.gov/sites/default/files/2022-10/22-088_EEOC_KnowYourRights_10_20.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;more information&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kikoff: The Fintech Powering Financial Security at Scale&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Kikoff is a profitable, pre-IPO fintech company on a mission to empower everyone to achieve financial security. With record revenue growth in 2025 and a unicorn valuation, we&#39;ve built a suite of products that help millions of people build credit, access liquidity, and save money.&lt;br&gt;We&#39;re scaling fast. Join us if you want to build something meaningful and help millions of people move forward financially.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Kikoff:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a consumer fintech startup, and you will be working with serial entrepreneurs who have built strong consumer brands and innovative products. We value extreme ownership, clear communication, a strong sense of craftsmanship, and the desire to create lasting work and work relationships. Yes, you can build an exciting business AND have real-life real-customer impact.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an Affiliate Marketing Manager to join our Business team. This isn’t just a &quot;client-facing&quot; role; it’s a hybrid of digital marketing strategy and data analysis. You will own a set of partners, define growth strategy and optimization paths, and collaborate closely with the User Acquisition team on achieving growth goals.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll own&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;North Star Objectives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion Kikoff’s products and services and become the influential main point of contact for our active partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Heavily contribute to Kikoff’s ambitious new user acquisition goals through account management, up/cross selling, and optimizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consistently overachieve monthly acquisition goals and grow your career as a contributing member of Kikoff&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Affiliate Relationship Management:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the main point of contact for assigned affiliate partners, fostering strong and collaborative relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate regularly with affiliates partners to understand their needs, provide support, and address any concerns or issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a liaison between affiliates and internal teams to ensure alignment on goals, promotions, and campaign strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage central inboxes to answer common questions and provide support to existing and inquiring partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft compelling recruitment pitches and partner newsletters that excite partners and drive action&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Campaign Management and Optimization:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with affiliate partners to develop and execute effective marketing campaigns that drive traffic, conversions, and revenue&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor campaign performance, analyze data, and identify opportunities for optimization and improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present strategic guidance and recommendations to partners to help them maximize their performance and reach their goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performance Tracking and Reporting:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and analyze key performance metrics such as clicks, conversions, and revenue generated by affiliate partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare regular reports (monthly, weekly) and updates on affiliate program performance to share with internal stakeholders and affiliates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide insights and recommendations based on data analysis to drive decision-making and improve campaign effectiveness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Synthesize and share creative learnings from campaigns with cross-functional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Marketing, Business, or related field preferred (or in progress)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1-3 years of experience in affiliate marketing, account management, or a related role (affiliate agency experience a plus)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of affiliate marketing principles, strategies, and best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication, writing, and interpersonal skills, with the ability to build rapport and trust with affiliate partners and cross-functional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to manage multiple projects and priorities in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical mindset with the ability to interpret data, draw insights, and make data-driven decisions; proficiency with data software such as Tableau and Amplitude&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with affiliate tracking platforms and tools (e.g., Impact, Appsflyer), proficiency in Excel/Google Sheets (Pivot Tables, VLOOKUPs), and familiarity with AI automation (Claude Cowork, Claude Code)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-motivated, proactive, and results-oriented, with a commitment to delivering exceptional service and results and brings a “test and learn” approach&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with DTC, subscription, or fintech a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Base Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$110,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$125,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A note on applying:&lt;/strong&gt; We know great candidates sometimes hold back if they don’t meet every qualification listed. If you’re excited about this role and believe you can do the work, we encourage you to apply. We’re looking for capability and trajectory, not a perfect checklist match.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;Equal Employment Opportunity Statement&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Kikoff Inc. is an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to complying with all federal, state, and local laws providing equal employment opportunities and considers qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, creed, gender, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy, sex, gender expression or identity, sexual orientation, citizenship, or any other legally protected class.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please reference the following for &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.eeoc.gov/sites/default/files/2022-10/22-088_EEOC_KnowYourRights_10_20.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;more information&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kikoff: The Fintech Powering Financial Security at Scale&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Kikoff is a profitable, pre-IPO fintech company on a mission to empower everyone to achieve financial security. With record revenue growth in 2025 and a unicorn valuation, we&#39;ve built a suite of products that help millions of people build credit, access liquidity, and save money.&lt;br&gt;We&#39;re scaling fast. Join us if you want to build something meaningful and help millions of people move forward financially.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Kikoff:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a consumer fintech startup, and you will be working with serial entrepreneurs who have built strong consumer brands and innovative products. We value extreme ownership, clear communication, a strong sense of craftsmanship, and the desire to create lasting work and work relationships. Yes, you can build an exciting business AND have real-life real-customer impact.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About this role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Associate Program Manager, CX, you&#39;ll shape how millions of customers experience Kikoff end to end, turning customer insight into the systems and improvements that make every interaction better. You&#39;ll pinpoint the highest-impact gaps, decide where AI automation, CX tooling, and measurement will move the needle for customers and the business, and take solutions from idea to completion in order to drive measurable impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This isn’t a frontline support role. Our Customer Support team handles tickets, and your job is to build the systems and processes that make their work easier and the customer’s experience better. When part of the product is causing friction, you’ll bring the data, work with Product and Engineering to fix the root cause, and help define how we measure CX, including contact rate, CSAT, and customer risk signals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-ownership role with exposure to strategic questions and a primary focus on execution: building systems that scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Role &amp;amp; responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Automation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build our AI chatbot strategy (coverage, containment, resolution quality)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement automation beyond chatbots, including:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Agent-assist / &quot;copilot&quot; workflows to reduce manual effort and errors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automated servicing flows (e.g., follow-ups, status updates, issue resolution)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CX Tooling&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve and maintain core CX systems (e.g., Zendesk, workflows, CSAT collection)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support development of internal tools that increase agent and team efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help standardize tooling and workflows across support channels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Measurement &amp;amp; Insights&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze CX performance across channels (chatbot, support, product journeys)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify friction points not captured in support tickets (e.g., drop-offs, dead ends), and work with the Product team to resolve them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain dashboards to track key CX metrics and initiative impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-functional execution&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Customer Operations, Product, and Data teams to implement solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own initiatives end-to-end: problem definition → solution design → launch → measurement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate customer insights and data into actionable improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Expertise &amp;amp; experience required&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2–4 years experience in CX, Operations, Product Ops, Consulting, or similar roles, including hands-on customer experience or support operations work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with CX tools (Zendesk, chat platforms, CSAT tools)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and problem-solving skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate in ambiguous environments and drive execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working cross-functionally with Product, Engineering, or Operations teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High ownership and bias toward action&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to automation, workflows, or AI-driven tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building dashboards or working with data tools (SQL, Looker, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Base Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$132,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$155,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A note on applying:&lt;/strong&gt; We know great candidates sometimes hold back if they don’t meet every qualification listed. If you’re excited about this role and believe you can do the work, we encourage you to apply. We’re looking for capability and trajectory, not a perfect checklist match.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;Equal Employment Opportunity Statement&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Kikoff Inc. is an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to complying with all federal, state, and local laws providing equal employment opportunities and considers qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, creed, gender, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy, sex, gender expression or identity, sexual orientation, citizenship, or any other legally protected class.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please reference the following for &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.eeoc.gov/sites/default/files/2022-10/22-088_EEOC_KnowYourRights_10_20.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;more information&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kikoff: The Fintech Powering Financial Security at Scale&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Kikoff is a profitable, pre-IPO fintech company on a mission to empower everyone to achieve financial security. With record revenue growth in 2025 and a unicorn valuation, we&#39;ve built a suite of products that help millions of people build credit, access liquidity, and save money.&lt;br&gt;We&#39;re scaling fast. Join us if you want to build something meaningful and help millions of people move forward financially.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Kikoff:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a consumer fintech startup, and you will be working with serial entrepreneurs who have built strong consumer brands and innovative products. We value extreme ownership, clear communication, a strong sense of craftsmanship, and the desire to create lasting work and work relationships. Yes, you can build an exciting business AND have real-life real-customer impact.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a Creative Director to lead our video and visual design teams and shape the next chapter of Kikoff’s creative, bringing exceptional creative judgment and a strong understanding of what makes performance advertising effective. You’ll help define our visual identity and lead evergreen performance creative across TV, paid social, and other marketing channels, making our brands more recognizable and driving efficient acquisition.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You bring exceptional taste, strong advertising instincts, and a clear point of view on what makes creative effective. You can see the potential in an idea and give specific direction that makes it stronger. You’re equally invested in developing people, helping creatives build their judgment, sharpen their craft, and take on greater ownership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Please include a portfolio featuring TV and paid social advertising, measurable results, and examples of a visual identity you helped define or evolve.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead creative direction for evergreen performance advertising across video and visual design. Turn consumer needs and product benefits into clear, compelling creative that drives acquisition and conversion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Brand leadership to define and evolve Kikoff’s visual identity. Translate brand strategy into a distinctive, practical system of design, imagery, and motion that makes our creative more consistent and recognizable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee creative across multiple brands and products, giving each a distinct expression while maintaining appropriate connections across the portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and coach the internal video and visual design teams. Build on individual strengths, develop creative judgment, and support growth through clear expectations, regular feedback, and thoughtful delegation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set creative standards across internal teams, freelance and contract resources, and our editing agency. Align priorities and capacity with business needs to deliver a high volume of effective work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Give specific, strategic feedback that strengthens both the idea and the execution. Help the team connect choices in messaging, design, and storytelling to the audience, consumer benefit, and desired action.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide design across paid social, digital marketing, and other brand touchpoints, strengthening layout, typography, and visual hierarchy to make product benefits clear and drive action.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help shape the creative vision for TV and video shoots in partnership with brand and production leads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide post-production across our internal editors and editing agency, with clear direction on narrative, pacing, motion, sound, and finishing to strengthen creative quality and effectiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Growth Marketing to understand priorities and apply the performance learnings they bring, continuously improving creative across concepts, messaging, and formats.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Creative Strategy, Copy, and Product Marketing to translate insights into effective advertising, and with Legal and Compliance to keep creative clear, accurate, and compliant.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years in advertising, design, or creative roles, including 5+ years managing and developing creative teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional taste and strong art direction skills across video and visual design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience defining or significantly evolving a brand’s visual identity and applying it consistently across channels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in evergreen performance creative, especially paid social, with a track record of driving measurable business results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;TV advertising experience and a strong portfolio spanning TV and paid social, with clear examples of your role and impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong post-production experience, including directing editors and giving actionable feedback on edits, motion, sound, and finishing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strategic approach that connects creative choices to consumer needs, product benefits, and business objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to coach talent at different career stages and give specific feedback that develops both craft and judgment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience overseeing high-volume creative across multiple brands or products and a mix of internal and external resources.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to translate performance insights into stronger creative and collaborate effectively with the Growth Marketing team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience using AI tools to improve creative exploration or workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with video production and experience collaborating with producers and production teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with UGC and creator-led advertising.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in consumer fintech or other regulated categories.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Base Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$163,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$225,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A note on applying:&lt;/strong&gt; We know great candidates sometimes hold back if they don’t meet every qualification listed. If you’re excited about this role and believe you can do the work, we encourage you to apply. We’re looking for capability and trajectory, not a perfect checklist match.&lt;/p&gt;
