&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kikoff: The Fintech Powering Financial Security at Scale&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Kikoff is a profitable, pre-IPO fintech company on a mission to empower everyone to achieve financial security. With record revenue growth in 2025 and a unicorn valuation, we&#39;ve built a suite of products that help millions of people build credit, access liquidity, and save money.&lt;br&gt;We&#39;re scaling fast. Join us if you want to build something meaningful and help millions of people move forward financially.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Kikoff:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a consumer fintech startup, and you will be working with serial entrepreneurs who have built strong consumer brands and innovative products. We value extreme ownership, clear communication, a strong sense of craftsmanship, and the desire to create lasting work and work relationships. Yes, you can build an exciting business AND have real-life real-customer impact.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Grant:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Grant, a subsidiary of Kikoff, is revolutionizing financial access through our intelligent earned wage access (EWA) product. We&#39;re solving real customer pain points by providing fast, fair access to earned wages when life happens, without the predatory fees common in the industry.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Kikoff is seeking its first government affairs leader to shape and advance the company&#39;s public policy agenda at the federal and state levels for Grant, its earned wage access (EWA) product. You will be Grant&#39;s primary voice with legislators, regulators, trade associations, consumer advocates, and other stakeholders, and you will lead strategy to support a clear, workable legal framework for EWA. This is a high-impact, hands-on role for someone who builds durable relationships, translates policy into business strategy, and is comfortable operating in a fast-moving, evolving regulatory landscape.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role will involve regular nationwide travel.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute Grant’s government affairs strategy, with an initial focus on federal and state policy affecting earned wage access and consumer credit-building products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Grant before legislators, legislative staff, federal and state financial regulators, attorneys general, and other public officials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as Grant’s representative to relevant trade associations and industry coalitions, taking active roles on committees and working groups and helping shape industry positions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain constructive relationships with consumer advocacy groups, community organizations, think tanks, and other stakeholders, including those who may hold differing views.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor, analyze, and report on legislative and regulatory developments; assess business impact and recommend responses, including testimony, comment letters, and model legislative language, in coordination with Legal and Compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, hire, and manage outside lobbyists and consultants across priority states and at the federal level, including setting objectives, overseeing budgets, and evaluating performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise executive leadership and the communications team on public relations positioning, messaging, and reputational considerations related to policy issues and regulatory developments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Legal, Compliance, Product, and Executive teams to ensure policy strategy aligns with business priorities and product roadmaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee compliance with lobbying registration, reporting, and political activity rules, in coordination with Legal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Grant Kikoff at hearings, conferences, industry events, and stakeholder meetings nationwide.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4–10 years of experience in government affairs, public policy, legislative or regulatory affairs, or advocacy, gained in-house, at a trade association, at a public affairs firm, or in government service.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A self-starter with a founder’s mindset and is comfortable establishing and honing processes where little internal infrastructure exists&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated track record of building and leveraging relationships with policymakers, regulators, and stakeholders at the state and/or federal level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing and executing multi-state legislative or regulatory strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience engaging, directing, and managing outside lobbyists or consultants.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in fintech, consumer financial services, or payments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to distill complex financial and regulatory issues for diverse audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound judgment on messaging and public positioning; comfort advising senior leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently and manage competing priorities in a fast-paced, high-growth environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel nationally as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with earned wage access, consumer lending, or credit-reporting policy issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with fintech or financial services trade associations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Existing relationships with state financial regulators, state legislators, the CFPB, or other federal financial agencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree or higher in public policy, political science, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
