&lt;p&gt;Kikoff Inc. is an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to complying with all federal, state, and local laws providing equal employment opportunities and considers qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, creed, gender, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy, sex, gender expression or identity, sexual orientation, citizenship, or any other legally protected class.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please reference the following for &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.eeoc.gov/sites/default/files/2022-10/22-088_EEOC_KnowYourRights_10_20.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;more information&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kikoff: The Fintech Powering Financial Security at Scale&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Kikoff is a profitable, pre-IPO fintech company on a mission to empower everyone to achieve financial security. With record revenue growth in 2025 and a unicorn valuation, we&#39;ve built a suite of products that help millions of people build credit, access liquidity, and save money.&lt;br&gt;We&#39;re scaling fast. Join us if you want to build something meaningful and help millions of people move forward financially.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Kikoff:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a consumer fintech startup, and you will be working with serial entrepreneurs who have built strong consumer brands and innovative products. We value extreme ownership, clear communication, a strong sense of craftsmanship, and the desire to create lasting work and work relationships. Yes, you can build an exciting business AND have real-life real-customer impact.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Manager, Business Development - Enterprise&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Kikoff Enterprise helps businesses turn credit progression into a driver of customer and business growth. Through Kikoff&#39;s embedded credit products and infrastructure, partners can help their customers build stronger credit while creating opportunities to expand eligibility, deepen engagement, improve retention, and unlock access to additional financial products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Business Development team is responsible for bringing this value proposition to market. We identify strategic partners, understand the business problems they are trying to solve, design solutions using Kikoff&#39;s Enterprise platform, and build the commercial relationships required to bring those solutions to life.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our partners span financial institutions, lenders, fintech and embedded finance platforms, gig economy companies, and other large consumer businesses. Partnerships can range from embedding Kikoff&#39;s credit-building products into a partner&#39;s customer experience to powering critical credit infrastructure such as bureau furnishing, decline recovery, dispute management, decisioning, and credit progression.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team works closely with executive leadership and cross-functional partners across Product, Engineering, Marketing, Operations, Legal, Compliance, and Finance. By joining this team, you will play a key role in defining and scaling Kikoff Enterprise as a major growth engine for the company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Senior Manager, Business Development to help define and scale Kikoff&#39;s Enterprise business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a highly strategic role responsible for developing some of Kikoff&#39;s largest and most consequential partnerships. You will own complex opportunities from initial strategy and executive engagement through commercial agreement, launch, and long-term expansion.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Rather than selling a predefined product, you will develop a deep understanding of a partner&#39;s business, identify where credit progression and Kikoff&#39;s infrastructure can create meaningful economic value, and architect solutions that benefit both the partner and its customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be expected to develop strong points of view on new markets, partners, and business models; build the business case for pursuing them; and mobilize teams across Kikoff to turn those opportunities into scalable businesses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a senior member of the Enterprise team, you will also help shape Kikoff&#39;s go-to-market strategy, influence the Enterprise product roadmap, establish best practices for strategic partnerships, and serve as a trusted partner to senior executives both internally and externally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join the Kikoff Business Development Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Help build a major new business at Kikoff.&lt;/strong&gt; Enterprise represents an opportunity to extend Kikoff&#39;s products and infrastructure to millions of consumers through some of the largest financial and consumer platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own high-impact strategic partnerships.&lt;/strong&gt; Work on relationships that can materially influence Kikoff&#39;s distribution, product strategy, and long-term growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Create value beyond distribution.&lt;/strong&gt; Help partners use credit progression to expand their addressable markets, recover declined customers, deepen engagement, improve product eligibility, increase retention, and unlock new revenue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shape the strategy, not just execute it.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ll help determine which markets Kikoff enters, which partners we prioritize, and how we structure new Enterprise products and business models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work directly with senior leadership.&lt;/strong&gt; This role operates across executive teams at Kikoff and our partners and has significant visibility throughout the organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Take proven capabilities into new markets.&lt;/strong&gt; Build enterprise businesses around Kikoff&#39;s consumer products, credit infrastructure, data, and technology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Grow with the organization.&lt;/strong&gt; As the Enterprise business expands, this role has meaningful opportunity to take on broader commercial and team leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own Kikoff&#39;s most strategic and complex Enterprise opportunities from market development and executive engagement through negotiation, launch, and long-term expansion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a deep understanding of prospective partners&#39; businesses, customers, economics, strategic priorities, and product roadmaps to identify where Kikoff can create differentiated value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain relationships with senior executives across banks, credit unions, lenders, fintechs, embedded finance platforms, and large consumer businesses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop tailored partnership strategies that connect Kikoff&#39;s capabilities to partner objectives such as market expansion, customer acquisition, credit eligibility, decline recovery, engagement, retention, cross-sell, and monetization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build sophisticated business cases and commercial models that quantify the value of a partnership for both Kikoff and the partner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead complex negotiations involving partnership economics, product scope, integrations, data, go-to-market strategy, and long-term commercial structures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and develop new industries, channels, use cases, and partnership models that can materially expand Kikoff&#39;s addressable market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop points of view on market opportunities and make recommendations to Kikoff&#39;s leadership team regarding where the Enterprise business should invest.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Product and Engineering leadership to translate market opportunities and partner needs into scalable Enterprise products and infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence Kikoff&#39;s Enterprise roadmap by identifying recurring partner needs and distinguishing between strategic platform capabilities and one-off customization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-functional teams across Product, Engineering, Legal, Compliance, Finance, Operations, Marketing, and Growth to move complex partnerships from concept to launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the strategic growth of major partners after launch, identifying additional products, customer segments, distribution opportunities, and commercial models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish executive-level operating rhythms and business reviews with strategic partners to drive accountability and identify opportunities for expansion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a senior voice of the market internally, bringing competitive intelligence, partner feedback, and emerging industry trends into Kikoff&#39;s product and corporate strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help establish the processes, frameworks, and operating principles required to scale Kikoff&#39;s Enterprise partnership organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and support more junior members of the Business Development team and raise the overall quality of strategic thinking, deal execution, and partner management across the organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree and 6-8+ years of experience across business development, strategic partnerships, fintech, financial services, corporate development, management consulting, investment banking, or similarly strategic and analytical roles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong fintech or financial services background, with a sophisticated understanding of the ecosystem across consumer credit, lending, banking, embedded finance, payments, or financial infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience developing and managing strategic relationships with financial institutions, fintech platforms, lenders, or other complex and regulated businesses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of originating, structuring, negotiating, and scaling large, complex partnerships with meaningful commercial impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working directly with senior executives and the ability to establish credibility quickly with C-suite and business-unit leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional strategic and commercial judgment, with the ability to understand how a partner&#39;s business works, identify where Kikoff can create value, and turn that insight into a scalable partnership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with B2B and/or B2B2C, embedded finance, API-based, platform, or other ecosystem business models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong consultative approach and the ability to lead discovery around a partner&#39;s business problems rather than relying on a predefined product pitch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced quantitative and financial skills, including experience building business cases, financial models, market-sizing analyses, and complex commercial structures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong negotiation skills and experience navigating deals involving multiple stakeholders, competing priorities, and complex product or regulatory considerations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to influence Product, Engineering, Legal, Compliance, Finance, Operations, and Go-to-Market teams without direct authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to distill complex business and technical concepts into clear executive-level narratives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience identifying and developing entirely new markets, channels, products, or partnership models is strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable operating with significant autonomy and ambiguity, forming a point of view with imperfect information, and driving an organization toward action.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated leadership and ability to mentor other team members, establish best practices, and raise the quality of execution across a growing organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with tools such as Salesforce or HubSpot, ZoomInfo, PitchBook or CB Insights, Tableau, Amplitude, Snowflake, and modern AI tools is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Base Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$170,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$198,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A note on applying:&lt;/strong&gt; We know great candidates sometimes hold back if they don’t meet every qualification listed. If you’re excited about this role and believe you can do the work, we encourage you to apply. We’re looking for capability and trajectory, not a perfect checklist match.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;Equal Employment Opportunity Statement&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Kikoff Inc. is an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to complying with all federal, state, and local laws providing equal employment opportunities and considers qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, creed, gender, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy, sex, gender expression or identity, sexual orientation, citizenship, or any other legally protected class.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please reference the following for &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.eeoc.gov/sites/default/files/2022-10/22-088_EEOC_KnowYourRights_10_20.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;more information&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kikoff: The Fintech Powering Financial Security at Scale&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Kikoff is a profitable, pre-IPO fintech company on a mission to empower everyone to achieve financial security. With record revenue growth in 2025 and a unicorn valuation, we&#39;ve built a suite of products that help millions of people build credit, access liquidity, and save money.&lt;br&gt;We&#39;re scaling fast. Join us if you want to build something meaningful and help millions of people move forward financially.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Kikoff:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a consumer fintech startup, and you will be working with serial entrepreneurs who have built strong consumer brands and innovative products. We value extreme ownership, clear communication, a strong sense of craftsmanship, and the desire to create lasting work and work relationships. Yes, you can build an exciting business AND have real-life real-customer impact.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the VP Corporate Controller, you will own Kikoff&#39;s external reporting and technical accounting as we prepare to go public. This is a founding hire: our technical accounting authority from day one, owning the financial statements and building the processes we will run as a public company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The scope is wider than a typical reporting role. Consumer credit receivables, cash advances, subscription revenue, bank partnerships, and structured financing all sit on our balance sheet, and each raises real accounting questions. You will own all of them except revenue recognition, which belongs to our revenue accounting lead. You will also own the reporting our lenders and bank partner require, and the ESG reporting we will grow into.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work closely with the VP Corporate Controller, CFO, external auditors, technical advisors, and internal and outside counsel, and you can build a team as we scale. We want national office–caliber technical judgment paired with an operator&#39;s drafting ability, and someone who finds building from scratch energizing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role starts as an individual contributor and is based in our San Francisco office three days a week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SEC Reporting and IPO Readiness&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft the financial statement sections of our registration statements — financial statements, footnotes, MD&amp;amp;A, and supporting schedules — and run the tie-out process behind the auditors&#39; comfort letter.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and run the quarterly and annual reporting process — 10-Q, 10-K, 8-K, and proxy — including the close-to-file calendar, disclosure checklists, and XBRL tagging. Own the age-of-financial-statements limits that determine when we can go effective.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the shift from private to public accounting: emerging growth company and smaller reporting company status, the transition period election, unwinding private company alternatives, and standing up the new public company disclosures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Accounting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own technical accounting for everything except revenue recognition — document positions in audit-ready memos on stock compensation and pre-IPO equity valuation (ASC 718), EPS (ASC 260), segments (ASC 280), internal-use software (ASC 350-40), business combinations (ASC 805), debt (ASC 470), leases (ASC 842), related party transactions, and contingencies (ASC 450 and 460).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the credit and financing questions: sale versus secured borrowing on our warehouse and securitization facilities (ASC 860), consolidation and VIE analysis for financing vehicles and bank partner structures (ASC 810), and fair value measurement and fair value option elections (ASC 820 and 825). We want you in these deals before documents are signed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track new accounting standards and SEC rulemaking, flag what matters to leadership, and start implementation early — including ASU 2024-03 (expense disaggregation), ASU 2025-08 (purchased loans), and ASU 2025-06 (internal-use software).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner, Lender, and Regulatory Reporting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the recurring reporting our bank partner, warehouse lenders, and securitization investors require: program financial reporting, covenant compliance certificates, financial statement delivery, and reconciling loan tapes and servicer reports to the general ledger.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep a crosswalk between contract definitions — tangible net worth, EBITDA, eligible receivable, delinquency, charge-off — and their GAAP sources, and check every new standard against our covenants before we adopt it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be the accounting bridge to Compliance and Legal: own the financial data behind state licensing filings, size loss contingencies and remediation accruals (ASC 450), and make sure partner and regulatory submissions tie to the general ledger. Compliance owns the consumer programs — fair lending, FCRA, UDAAP, BSA/AML — you own the financial reporting behind them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track California SB 253 and SB 261 and other climate disclosure rules and assess when they apply to us. Support Legal and Investor Relations on voluntary ESG, impact, and SASB disclosures, make sure any metric we publish ties to the audited financials, and build the data trail so it holds up if assurance is ever required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Disclosure, Controls, and Building the Function&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set up the disclosure committee, the sub-certification process, and the documentation behind SOX 302 certifications. Partner with the SOX Director on reporting controls, and own the controls this function runs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define our non-GAAP measures and reconciliations and keep them Reg G and Item 10(e) compliant. Work with FP&amp;amp;A and Investor Relations so our operating metrics mean the same thing in the registration statement, earnings releases, and investor materials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the external auditors on reporting and technical matters — position papers, quarterly reviews, the annual audit, and the comfort letter.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set up how the function runs — tools, templates, and review cadence — and lead the hires that follow as the team grows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years across Big 4 public accounting and in-house SEC reporting or technical accounting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CPA required, with deep knowledge of US GAAP and SEC reporting rules, including Regulation S-X and S-K.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have personally drafted 10-Ks and 10-Qs, and ideally an S-1 or been through an IPO.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable with pre-IPO equity accounting — options and RSUs (ASC 718), 409A and cheap stock, and EPS on conversion of preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong research and memo-writing skills, and able to defend a position to auditors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable as an individual contributor now, with the judgment to know when to scale the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A clear communicator — you can turn a complex conclusion into a clean memo and explain it to non-accountants.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Workiva (or similar) and NetSuite experience preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience reporting to counterparties — covenant certificates, borrowing base or servicer reporting, or securitization reporting — and comfort turning contract definitions into GAAP.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Some exposure to ESG reporting — SB 253 and SB 261, TCFD, or SASB — or the appetite to learn it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lending, consumer credit, banking, or other regulated financial services experience preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Base Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$167,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$215,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A note on applying:&lt;/strong&gt; We know great candidates sometimes hold back if they don’t meet every qualification listed. If you’re excited about this role and believe you can do the work, we encourage you to apply. We’re looking for capability and trajectory, not a perfect checklist match.&lt;/p&gt;
